      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T18:56:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we always use a shared_ptr, can we get rid of the weak pointer?  I think we can check the reference count and only run the callback if the count is greater than 1.",
      "parentUuid": "adc1ca5e_7b6f29dc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 75
      },
      "revId": "7ea5f67ca8c063bd2c5c8be64157a1fbefae8c93",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
