      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T19:36:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess not, because to check the reference count we need the shared_pointer to still be valid and without a weak_pointer we don\u0027t hold any reference to the object so it could be destructed in between.\n\nHowever we could use a shared_from_this instead and hold a strong reference. But I\u0027m not sure that\u0027s what we want to do.",
      "parentUuid": "bf568dd3_08aec311",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 55,
        "endChar": 75
      },
      "revId": "7ea5f67ca8c063bd2c5c8be64157a1fbefae8c93",
