      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-11T08:25:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We do not care about executing the task callback for a controller that was dropped everywhere else, so it does not make sense to hold a strong (shared_ptr) reference to this. Instead the weak reference (weak_ptr) allows us to safely check if the controller was deleted and drop the callback in this case.\n\nAs far as I could tell DualModeController (or the inheriting class HciDevice) is always created behind a shared_ptr.",
      "parentUuid": "5b98fe1d_ad3b3e04",
